    <!-- Apotheosis: ONE SDK for both architectures since 2026-08-17, and it has to be 19041.
         Never "upgrade" it: SDK 10.0.26100.0 ships NO `um\arm` / `ucrt\arm` (verified: arm64/x64/x86
         only), so a Release|ARM build would resolve WindowsApp.lib to nothing. 19041 is the last SDK
         carrying all four target arches, and it is what `Src\port\arm32-uwp-env.ps1:12` pins for the
         ARM32 engine line.
         Two myths are buried here, both measured rather than assumed. First, Doc/Summary.md records
         "19041 is missing the XAML compiler DLL" as the reason x64 moved to 26100; that is wrong, the
         DLL is present and full size in bin\10.0.19041.0\XamlCompiler, alongside the UAP platform,
         Windows.winmd and 88 contract references. Second, an attempt to move x64 to 19041 earlier the
         same day did fail, but for a real and different reason: 19041 guards LoadLibraryExA,
         LoadLibraryA, GetModuleHandleA and GetModuleHandleW out of WINAPI_PARTITION_APP, while 26100
         declares them unguarded, and the harness called all four (the ICU 75 probe, the module base
         log, the EGL probe). Those call sites now use LoadPackagedLibrary and the linker-provided
         __ImageBase, so the harness is 19041 clean. The CompileXaml MSB4181 failure seen in that first
         attempt was a cascade of those compile errors, not an SDK defect: with the call sites fixed,
         a full 19041 build of every harness translation unit produces a byte-identical-sized appx
         (51.21 MB, 50 payload files) that installs and runs.
         The payoff is that both architectures finally run the SAME XAML compiler, so the generated
         MainPage.g.hpp is correct for both. It must still be included and never frozen, for the
         reasons in CLAUDE.md and Doc/UNIFICATION.md section C.
         Note that the x64 *engine* line is still on 26100 (`Src\setenv.ps1` APOTHEOSIS_SDK_VER,
         `Src\port\x64-uwp-env.ps1`, and build-x64-gpu's CMakeCache), so 26100 cannot be uninstalled
         until those are reconfigured. See Doc/UNIFICATION.md Track B.
         (XML comments cannot contain a double dash, which is why this one has none.) -->
    <WindowsTargetPlatformVersion>10.0.19041.0</WindowsTargetPlatformVersion>
    <WindowsTargetPlatformMinVersion>10.0.14393.0</WindowsTargetPlatformMinVersion>
    <!-- Apotheosis: pin the MSVC toolset so adding the ARM32 component in the VS Installer
         (which may drop a NEWER v143 toolset next to this one and flip the default stamp in
         VC\Auxiliary\Build\Microsoft.VCToolsVersion.v143.default.props) cannot silently move the
         x64 harness onto a different STL/CRT. Both build lines already hardcode 14.44.35207
         (setenv.ps1:21, arm32-uwp-env.ps1) — MSBuild was the only unpinned consumer.
         Today this equals the installed default, so it is a provable no-op. -->
    <VCToolsVersion>14.44.35207</VCToolsVersion>
